      "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}{log}_{5}⁡(x-2).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{5}⁡(x-2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274353/assets/42585a4ff6db9c4848588f10ac50bc78aa4d902ddacdb201039aa7a558d3a3a9.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\le 2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}{log}_{5}⁡(x-2)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x>2.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}{log}_{5}⁡(x-2)=-\\infty .\n$$",
